       "            degree: int or tuple (min_degree, max_degree), default=2<br><br>If a single int is given, it specifies the maximal degree of the<br>polynomial features. If a tuple `(min_degree, max_degree)` is passed,<br>then `min_degree` is the minimum and `max_degree` is the maximum<br>polynomial degree of the generated features. Note that `min_degree=0`<br>and `min_degree=1` are equivalent as outputting the degree zero term is<br>determined by `include_bias`.</span>\n",
